scm@harvee.billerica.ma.us (S. Mudgett aka little gator) writes:



>what does a cloak of displacement do?

When you wear it, it makes monsters more likely to miss when they try to
hit you.

>what does blessed or cursed mean, when it's not armor or a weapon?

It depends. For example some cursed potions and scrolls act completely
opposite to the uncursed or blessed ones, some blessed ones are more powerful
than uncursed ones.. in some cases it means almost nothing..
With rings it means exactly the same as with armor/weapon.

>i know statues can be weilded, but are they good (or bad) for anything else?

You may find it out with a pick-axe..

>what's the significance of lembas wafers?

They are food. (As you may guess since they are represented with a %).

>what's the point of chatting with monsters?

Try to #chat with temple priests..

>what is the benefit of putting stuff in a sack? and are boxes, chests, good
>for anything but looting?

Simply, you can carry more stuff. You see, there is a limited number of
inventory slots, only letters a-z and A-Z.. and when you put something in a
sack, it doesn't need an inventory letter. And there are special bags..
